# MAJORANA — Termux Edge Fleet and Sync Protocol

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant Cloud as WANGA Cloud API
  participant Queue as Signed Job Queue
  participant T1 as Termux Node A
  participant T2 as Termux Node B
  participant Audit as Audit / Decision Gate
  participant Repo as GitHub Canonical Repo
  Cloud->>Queue: Publish bounded signed task
  T1->>Cloud: Pull tasks with sync cursor
  Cloud-->>T1: Manifest + schema + expiry
  T1->>T1: Verify signature / allowlist / idempotency
  T1->>T1: Capture source + provenance + SHA-256
  T1->>Cloud: Push JSONL + artifact refs + receipt
  Cloud->>Audit: Validate source, schema and anti-drift
  Audit-->>Cloud: CANDIDATE / ABSTAIN / HUMAN_REVIEW
  Cloud->>Repo: Proposed delta via branch/PR after approval
  T2->>Cloud: Register independently
  T2->>Cloud: Pull its own scoped task
```

Termux nodes are edge workers, not canonical authorities. Default to outbound HTTPS, local SQLite queue, signed task manifests, allowlisted operations, idempotent retries and explicit human approval for core changes.